drm: h713-afbd: preserve progressive proc line start

ProcWinNode::CalcWindow at 0x8b1a5b50 derives line start as input VS delay
plus one, upstream vertical start, and the MB420 format term. The logged
39-line start belongs to an interlaced/deinterlaced path with input delay 15;
the progressive path has delay 3 and start 27. Vertical scaling alone does
not justify changing that upstream timing. Document why it is preserved.

Cold-boot tests of both start values retained the grey streak. This patch
does not claim to fix that artifact.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -388,11 +388,12 @@
 	/*
 	 * ProcWinNode::WriteReg writes output width twice and arms the second
 	 * copy with bit 31. More subtly, FRAME_LINES names the number of source
-	 * lines the vertical engine may consume. Leaving its native 720 there
-	 * makes a 544-line source finish early and exposes the fill colour.
-	 * Preserve the upper start-line field: it is accumulated latency from
-	 * the firmware-owned upstream pipeline, which this driver does not
-	 * reconfigure.
+	 * lines the vertical engine may consume in the low half. Preserve the
+	 * upper start-line field from the firmware-owned upstream pipeline.
+	 * CalcWindow derives it from input VS delay, upstream vertical start,
+	 * and the MB420 format term. The firmware's 39-line interlaced path
+	 * does not establish extra latency for progressive vertical scaling;
+	 * this progressive AFBD route retains its boot-time start (27).
 	 */
 	h713_proc_rmw(h, PROC_OUT_W_DUP, BIT(31) | PROC_FIELD16_MASK,
 		      BIT(31) | out_w);
